% c226 (playability, brass endurance; Adler ch. 9, adler1 PDF 292: 'allow frequent intervals of rest for the brass players so their lips can recuperate'; adler2 PDF 8: frequent rests between passages): Tpt 3 rests 251-254 with Tpt 1-2 (c076, c087), so it no longer plays 247-279 (about 46 s of f-fff) without a bar's rest and the three trumpets enter the last chorale together at 255; the timpani keep the strokes at 251 and 254.
% c316 (playability; Adler adler1 PDF 292, 309: loud slow phrases need breaths; Hn 3 breathes after 256): 258|259 Tpt 3 breathes before the crescendo; 255-264 (ten bars ff-fff, 12.6 s) had no breath mark.
% c374 (orchestration; Rimsky-Korsakov ch. III, PDF 102-103: 'Discords of the seventh or second are preferably entrusted to instruments of different tone colour'; PDF 100: brass part writing in close order): 249 Tpt 3's hammered strokes A4 (were C5). Under the F2 head in Tpt 1-2 (F5-E5-D5, D5-C5-A4) the C5 made a major second with Tpt 2's D5 on beat 1 and with Tpt 1's D5 on beat 3, and crossed above Tpt 2's A4 there, so the trumpet trio sounded F5/D5/C5 and D5/C5/A4. Now F5/D5/A4 and D5/A4/A4; the C stays in the timpani's strokes on the same rhythm (a different colour), A4 doubles Hn 3. Tpt 3's line C5-F4-A4-G4; tune, rhythm, dynamics unchanged.
