% c021: 265-268 trumpets 1-2 (a2) join horns 1-2 and violas on F1 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 72, 74: trumpet over trombones in octaves; it no longer hammers C5 on top of the theme's head note)
% c019: 255-262 horn 3 and trumpet 3 repeat their chorale notes as marcato half notes (the alla-breve beat) with the violas' quarters and the basses' eighths under the held chorale (Rimsky-Korsakov Ex. 91, 98, 116: a sustained melody over repeated chords; Tchaikovsky 5/iv, the major motto over pulsing wind chords). Hn 4 stays held: low stems below the staff push the score to 17 pages.
% c024 (orchestration; Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 51, 375, 505-507): 265-268 Hn 3-4 and Tbn 1-2 f under the ff F1 (doubling below, Ex. 209); 269-272 they join Hn 1-2, Bn 1, violas and cellos on movement I's head, so the two heads are balanced and in separate registers (F1 above in winds, Tpt 1-2, violins). 263 G added in Cl 2 and Vln II (fifth in the upper parts, PDF 85-86). 274 timpani C (the pedal). 278 trumpets C5-G4-E4, Tpt 1 on top.
% c074 (orchestration; Adler ch. 5, PDF 135-136, 152: spacing and doubling of the chord, background not re-attacking the melody's pitch): 257-258 Hn 3 C4 (was E4, the fifth brass part on the
% chorale's E4; the chord's third C had only Tbn 2 in the brass).
% c084 (Casanelles PDF 289: the brass are the foregrounded layer; A&S passing 8-7): 262 Hn 3 G4-F4, so the brass V7 of the last cadence has its 7th (it was G-B only in the brass), F4 -> E4 at 263
% c185 (Gould PDF 65-67: the upper part takes up-stems even when parts overlap, so a crossed pair reads as a chord; semibreves must not appear joined to stems):
% at 259-260 Hn 3 (A-flat3, halves, up-stems) sat under Hn 4's whole C4, which looked like a two-note half chord. The players swap: Hn 3 keeps C4 from 257 and rises to E-flat4 at 261,
% Hn 4 descends A3 (257) - A-flat3 (259-261) - G3 (262). Same pitches and rhythms per staff, no crossing.
% c189 (A&S Unit 29, PDF 505: the German sixth's E flat is reached by step; Unit 24, PDF 405: the 7th C of the iio6/5 is the Ger6's common tone; A&S Unit 5): 259-260 Hn 3 D4 (was C4 after c184/c185), so Hn 3 steps D4-E flat4 into 261 instead of C4-E flat4 in parallel fifths with the bass F-A flat (Tuba, B.tbn, Bn 2, Cbsn, Vc, Cb, B.cl). Hn 4 keeps A flat3 (c184).
% c305 (Gould, Behind Bars ch. 2, PDF 66: keep noteheads separate; a semibreve must not appear joined to a stem; editions reverse the order so the semibreve is never beside a stem): score-only force-hshift at 251 (Hn 3-4) puts the semibreve on the stem-free side of the other part's note, 0.15-0.2 space apart
